From c117ea644a542168baa03757fbf6fe535d929644 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DaffyDabz <daffydabz@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 13:03:36 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 005/371] pirates: quests, NPC turn-in, shopkeeper (Sept 2026
 family-server fixes)

- QuestManagerAI: finalize cutscenes now play through the quest so the game
  state carries from one scene to the next (the pirate is no longer stuck in
  Dialog with the camera on the NPC), wait for the ship name when a scene needs
  it (never stalls more than two minutes), and close the NPC talk after the
  last scene. requestInteract reports whether the quest handled the talk. A
  dropped quest's stub no longer re-runs the ladder drop.
- DistributedQuestAvatarAI: quest tracking beam works for "defeat any enemy"
  goals and for world-data-only goals (Quest Node, Dinghy), is positioned
  relative to the goal's parent instead of riding with the player, and the
  journal's untrack is echoed back.
- DistributedQuestGiverAI: quest offers from the ladder, dependency and
  dynamic-map data for the giver.
- QuestTaskDNA: a task with no location can be done anywhere, so deliver
  quests can be handed in.
- DistributedQuest (client): a finalize cutscene waits for the tunnel walk-out
  to hand control back (15 s cap) before it starts.
- DistributedNPCTownfolkAI: talk plays the greeting line (flag 0, not the
  mid-quest TALK) and does not open the NPC menu when the talk just finished
  a quest.
- DistributedEnemySpawnerAI: remember the spawn uid as the quest giver id,
  even for NPCs with a CustomModel.
- DistributedShopKeeperAI: repair, overhaul and sell-ship requests (were
  `pass`) read the docked ship's saved fields and write the new values to the
  live object and the database.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
